    "reason": "evidence sufficient (proxy gate verdict; the open aspects need proposals): [ev-ebdf9bd62d77] says Kyverno Service API calls now support custom HTTP request headers, for example an Authorization token. The rendered CRD diffs [ev-99b53074f2f0, ev-4223a9a83b9a, ev-ca8925aad7a2, ev-9636947e7fb1, ev-60b490ef3d10] show a new field, apiCall.service.headers, appearing as a new field (∅ in 1.12.6) in 1.13.0. The schema describes it as a list of optional key/value headers. That pins down the subject, the change type (\"added\") and a consequence of \"none\" for existing setups. For the open applicability aspect, the evidence shows the field is new and optional with no default, so it only matters to environments that choose to set it; an engineer can record applicability as \"no existing environment exposed\" without guessing.",
